# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dehradun OBIA vs Pixel-Based — .gitignore
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Goal: keep ALL code, ALL maps/figures, the slide deck, the report, the
# accuracy tables and the small classified rasters — but exclude the huge
# source Sentinel-2 composites (~600 MB each, GitHub blocks > 100 MB).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Raw Sentinel-2 composites (1.2 GB total) -----------------------------
01_raw_data/Dehradun_2016.tif
01_raw_data/Dehradun_2024.tif
01_raw_data/*.aux.xml
01_raw_data/*.tif.ovr
# Keep the metadata CSV: it documents the GEE export.
!01_raw_data/Dehradun_S2_scene_metadata.csv

# --- Polygonised segment shapefiles (huge — segments_*.tif is the source) -
# The seg_*.shp/dbf/shx/prj quartet was generated by QGIS during exploration
# and reaches 1.4 GB. The authoritative segment store is segments_*.tif.
03_segmentation/seg_*.shp
03_segmentation/seg_*.shx
03_segmentation/seg_*.dbf
03_segmentation/seg_*.prj
03_segmentation/seg_*.cpg
03_segmentation/seg_*.qpj

# --- QGIS project file (binary, optional) --------------------------------
*.qgz~
*.qgs~

# --- Python build / cache -------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- IDE / OS noise -------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp

# --- Trained-model joblib files (regenerable, ~few MB each) ---------------
04_classification_OBIA/*.joblib
05_classification_pixel/*.joblib

# --- Intermediate "_v2" pptx fallbacks ------------------------------------
09_report_slides/*_v2.pptx
09_report_slides/*_v2.docx

# --- Large per-chip directories (40 PNGs each, optional to share) --------
# Comment out if you want them in the repo for documentation.
04_classification_OBIA/chips_2016/
04_classification_OBIA/chips_2024/
